# Trigger.dev Tasks

## Where things run

- Self-hosted Trigger.dev v4 on `the-keep`, never Trigger.dev cloud (D-003)
- The CLI and SDK find it through `LYTERION_TRIGGER_API_URL` (mapped to `TRIGGER_API_URL` by the root scripts)
- Env vars used inside tasks must be set on the self-hosted project environment, `pnpm deploy:trigger` does not sync `.env`

## Task pattern

```typescript
import { task } from "@trigger.dev/sdk";

export const acquireRecordingTask = task({
  id: "acquire.recording",
  queue: { name: "acquire", concurrencyLimit: 4 },
  run: async ({ recordingId }: { recordingId: string }) => {
    return acquireRecording(recordingId);
  },
});
```

- Task ids follow the pipeline names in `docs/pipeline.md` (`spotify.export`, `acquire.recording`, `navidrome.scan`...)
- Per-provider concurrency lives in named queues (`docs/providers.md` § Rate and concurrency)
- Idempotency keys per `docs/pipeline.md` § Idempotency
- No parent task waits hours on children: stages advance event-driven through DB counters (D-014)
- Progress per stage goes through a single `updateStageProgress` style helper, never a full JSONB overwrite

## LLM keys in tasks

Resolve models through `getAIModel(task)` from `@lyterion/ai-provider`, gate on `isProviderConfigured(task)`.
